00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:09.000
in the field of law by anybody,

cue0017613
00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:11.000
including the Romans, it was nothing like this.

cue0017614
00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:13.000
It was the Mishna.

cue0017615
00:25:13.000 --> 00:25:15.000
The Mishna comprises six

cue0017616
00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:17.000
orders.

cue0017617
00:25:17.000 --> 00:25:19.000
Each order had above

cue0017618
00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:21.000
ten volumes.

cue0017619
00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:23.000
Between

cue0017620
00:25:23.000 --> 00:25:25.000
these ten volumes, there is about

cue0017621
00:25:25.000 --> 00:25:27.000
five hundred and some

cue0017622
00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:29.000
chapters.

cue0017623
00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:31.000
Every chapter has

cue0017624
00:25:31.000 --> 00:25:33.000
about, say,

cue0017625
00:25:33.000 --> 00:25:35.000
twenty paragraphs.

cue0017626
00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:37.000
That means a collection of

cue0017627
00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:39.000
ten thousand paragraphs.

cue0017628
00:25:39.000 --> 00:25:41.000
Very concise,

cue0017629
00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:43.000
written almost in a formulaic

cue0017630
00:25:43.000 --> 00:25:45.000
way.

cue0017631
00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:47.000
Each word could be a

cue0017632
00:25:47.000 --> 00:25:49.000
treatise on each word.

cue0017633
00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:51.000
Each word

cue0017634
00:25:51.000 --> 00:25:53.000
of the Tora Shem Eateh.

cue0017635
00:25:53.000 --> 00:25:55.000
Now, that is the

cue0017636
00:25:55.000 --> 00:25:57.000
most important

cue0017637
00:25:57.000 --> 00:25:59.000
collection of Tora Shem Eateh.

cue0017638
00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:01.000
No nation, again,

cue0017639
00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:03.000
did a collection of Tora Shem Eateh.

cue0017640
00:26:03.000 --> 00:26:05.000
But in addition to this,

cue0017641
00:26:05.000 --> 00:26:07.000
there were

cue0017642
00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:09.000
three other collections.

cue0017643
00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:11.000
One of them

cue0017644
00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:13.000
is Siphraʾ.

cue0017645
00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:15.000
And those are collections of

cue0017646
00:26:15.000 --> 00:26:17.000
Tora Shem Eateh following the order

cue0017647
00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:19.000
of the Basur.

cue0017648
00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:21.000
Alright?

cue0017649
00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:23.000
And the Siphraʾ is in the book of Aikah.

cue0017650
00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:25.000
And then there is

cue0017651
00:26:25.000 --> 00:26:27.000
Shalom Uvracha Tovah.

cue0017652
00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:29.000
My good old friend.

cue0017653
00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:31.000
My old good friend.

cue0017654
00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:33.000
How are you doing?

cue0017655
00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:35.000
How's your family?

cue0017656
00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:37.000
How are you doing yourself?

cue0017657
00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:39.000
Your son?

cue0017658
00:26:39.000 --> 00:26:41.000
My son once got up to read

cue0017659
00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:43.000
today, and the other one went to New Jersey.

cue0017660
00:26:43.000 --> 00:26:45.000
Oh, well, I didn't want

cue0017661
00:26:45.000 --> 00:26:47.000
to find out how they do it.

cue0017662
00:26:47.000 --> 00:26:49.000
You look fine, also.

cue0017663
00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:51.000
Yes.

cue0017664
00:26:51.000 --> 00:26:53.000
Please, if you want to sit down,

cue0017665
00:26:53.000 --> 00:26:55.000
it would be my pleasure.

cue0017666
00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:09.000
So, we're talking

cue0017667
00:27:09.000 --> 00:27:11.000
about the Talmud,

cue0017668
00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:13.000
both the Babylonian

cue0017669
00:27:13.000 --> 00:27:15.000
and the Yerushalmi,

cue0017670
00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:17.000
the Israel Talmud.

cue0017671
00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:19.000
And I don't like

cue0017672
00:27:19.000 --> 00:27:21.000
some scholars,

cue0017673
00:27:21.000 --> 00:27:23.000
they use the word Palestinian Talmud.

cue0017674
00:27:23.000 --> 00:27:25.000
I don't like to use the word Palestinian Talmud.

cue0017675
00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:27.000
It's a horrible word.

cue0017676
00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:29.000
Yeah,

cue0017677
00:27:29.000 --> 00:27:31.000
especially now.

cue0017678
00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:33.000
So, what I was saying,

cue0017679
00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:35.000
I began at the very beginning,

cue0017680
00:27:35.000 --> 00:27:37.000
but just let me

cue0017681
00:27:37.000 --> 00:27:39.000
give you a point of preface.

cue0017682
00:27:39.000 --> 00:27:41.000
By the year 135 of the coming

cue0017683
00:27:41.000 --> 00:27:43.000
era,

cue0017684
00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:45.000
the Romans apparently,

cue0017685
00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:47.000
what scholars consider

cue0017686
00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:49.000
the study is that

cue0017687
00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:51.000
95% of the population

cue0017688
00:27:51.000 --> 00:27:53.000
in Yehuda,

cue0017689
00:27:53.000 --> 00:27:55.000
Judean population, the Jewish

cue0017690
00:27:55.000 --> 00:27:57.000
population in Judea, were exterminated

cue0017691
00:27:57.000 --> 00:27:59.000
by the Romans. 90%.

cue0017692
00:27:59.000 --> 00:28:01.000
Alright?

cue0017693
00:28:01.000 --> 00:28:03.000
90%. Not 70%,

cue0017694
00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:05.000
not 80%,

cue0017695
00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:07.000
not 60%, 90%.

cue0017696
00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:09.000
And these are the most recent studies

cue0017697
00:28:09.000 --> 00:28:11.000
made by Yehoshaphat Harkavi,

cue0017698
00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:13.000
who was a great scholar,

cue0017699
00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:15.000
and he was a general in the

cue0017700
00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:17.000
Israeli army,

cue0017701
00:28:17.000 --> 00:28:19.000
and he studied

cue0017702
00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:21.000
these battles

cue0017703
00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:23.000
very carefully,

cue0017704
00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:25.000
with a military and a scholarly mind,

cue0017705
00:28:25.000 --> 00:28:27.000
and that is the result

cue0017706
00:28:27.000 --> 00:28:29.000
of his scholarship.

cue0017707
00:28:29.000 --> 00:28:31.000
He may be wrong, but if he's wrong,

cue0017708
00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:33.000
it's by a few percenters here and there.

cue0017709
00:28:33.000 --> 00:28:35.000
This is a very...

cue0017710
00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:37.000
So, which means by the

cue0017711
00:28:37.000 --> 00:28:39.000
year 135,

cue0017712
00:28:39.000 --> 00:28:41.000
we find ourselves with other countries,

cue0017713
00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:43.000
I mean, not only in the control of the country,

cue0017714
00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:45.000
with an imperialistic

cue0017715
00:28:45.000 --> 00:28:47.000
government. Rome is

cue0017716
00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:49.000
an imperialistic government,

cue0017717
00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:51.000
and we refer to Rome

cue0017718
00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:53.000
three times a day.

cue0017719
00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:55.000
We don't call them Rome,

cue0017720
00:28:55.000 --> 00:28:57.000
because our

cue0017721
00:28:57.000 --> 00:28:59.000
fight is not against the Roman people,

cue0017722
00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:01.000
or the people of Rome,

cue0017723
00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:03.000
but about the political system,

cue0017724
00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:05.000
and we call it Malchut HaShah,

cue0017725
00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:07.000
which is an imperialistic government.

cue0017726
00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:09.000
Our war is not with the Italians,

cue0017727
00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:11.000
or Neapolitanos, or Sicilianos,

cue0017728
00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:13.000
or the people of Florence,

cue0017729
00:29:13.000 --> 00:29:15.000
or the people from Italy today.

cue0017730
00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:17.000
We are friends.

cue0017731
00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:19.000
We are against

cue0017732
00:29:19.000 --> 00:29:21.000
the imperial

cue0017733
00:29:21.000 --> 00:29:23.000
policies of Rome.

cue0017734
00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:25.000
Imperial Rome.

cue0017735
00:29:25.000 --> 00:29:27.000
And with all due respect to

cue0017736
00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:29.000
our Christian friends,

cue0017737
00:29:29.000 --> 00:29:31.000
Malchut HaShah has nothing to do against Christianity.

cue0017738
00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:33.000
It's against Malchut HaShah, which is imperial Rome.

cue0017739
00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:35.000
Nothing to do with the government.

cue0017740
00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:37.000
Some of the people say, no, it's anti-Christian.

cue0017741
00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:39.000
No, it's not anti-Christian.

cue0017742
00:29:39.000 --> 00:29:41.000
If it was anti-Christian, we would say it is anti-Christian.

cue0017743
00:29:41.000 --> 00:29:43.000
It is not.

cue0017744
00:29:43.000 --> 00:29:45.000
And it's not anti-Italian.

cue0017745
00:29:45.000 --> 00:29:47.000
When I say Malchut Italia,

cue0017746
00:29:47.000 --> 00:29:49.000
I'm going to say Malchut HaShah,

cue0017747
00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:51.000
which is very important.

cue0017748
00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:53.000
So, we were dominated

cue0017749
00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:55.000
by another country.

cue0017750
00:29:55.000 --> 00:29:57.000
We don't have our people.

cue0017751
00:29:57.000 --> 00:29:59.000
And the worst part,

cue0017752
00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:01.000
our legal tradition,

cue0017753
00:30:01.000 --> 00:30:03.000
which was preserved in the

cue0017754
00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:05.000
Sanhedrin,

cue0017755
00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:07.000
was never put into writing.

cue0017756
00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:09.000
One of the things, the first thing,

cue0017757
00:30:09.000 --> 00:30:11.000
Josephus says, the first thing that the

cue0017758
00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:13.000
Romans used to do

cue0017759
00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:15.000
when attacking the Jews,

cue0017760
00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:17.000
you know what it was?

cue0017761
00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:19.000
Burn the archives.

cue0017762
00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:21.000
Burn the archives.

cue0017763
00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:23.000
That's the first thing

cue0017764
00:30:23.000 --> 00:30:25.000
they would do. So, our archives were

cue0017765
00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:27.000
burned.

cue0017766
00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:29.000
They were destroyed.

cue0017767
00:30:29.000 --> 00:30:31.000
So, how do,

cue0017768
00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:33.000
how can we maintain our Judaism?

cue0017769
00:30:33.000 --> 00:30:35.000
So, the task of Rabbi 'Aqiba

cue0017770
00:30:35.000 --> 00:30:37.000
and his pupils

cue0017771
00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:39.000
was

cue0017772
00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:41.000
to collect

cue0017773
00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:43.000
the remnants

cue0017774
00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:45.000
of the oral tradition.

cue0017775
00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:47.000
Why was it called oral tradition?

cue0017776
00:30:47.000 --> 00:30:49.000
Simply because it was not written.

cue0017777
00:30:49.000 --> 00:30:51.000
People's memory, they say,

cue0017778
00:30:51.000 --> 00:30:53.000
well, I saw this, I heard this.

cue0017779
00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:55.000
Somebody told me this way.

cue0017780
00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:57.000
And out of

cue0017781
00:30:57.000 --> 00:30:59.000
the memory

cue0017782
00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:01.000
of the people,

cue0017783
00:31:01.000 --> 00:31:03.000
and those old people were survivors of the Holocaust.

cue0017784
00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:05.000
It was a Holocaust worse than our own

cue0017785
00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:07.000
modern Holocaust.

cue0017786
00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:09.000
The students of Rabbi 'Aqiba and his students

cue0017787
00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:11.000
collected

cue0017788
00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:13.000
the material

cue0017789
00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:15.000
that eventually was incorporated and made

cue0017790
00:31:15.000 --> 00:31:17.000
into the Mishna.

cue0017791
00:31:17.000 --> 00:31:19.000
The Mishna preserved

cue0017792
00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:21.000
the legal traditions

cue0017793
00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:23.000
of Israel.

cue0017794
00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:25.000
The Mishna composes

cue0017795
00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:27.000
60 volumes.

cue0017796
00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:29.000
Between the 60 volumes,

cue0017797
00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:31.000
there are about, a little bit over,

cue0017798
00:31:31.000 --> 00:31:33.000
it's about 510

cue0017799
00:31:33.000 --> 00:31:35.000
chapters.

cue0017800
00:31:35.000 --> 00:31:37.000
Every chapter has about 20 paragraphs.

cue0017801
00:31:37.000 --> 00:31:39.000
Which means

cue0017802
00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:41.000
in excess of 10,000 legal paragraphs

cue0017803
00:31:41.000 --> 00:31:43.000
collected

cue0017804
00:31:43.000 --> 00:31:45.000
out of the memory of the people.

cue0017805
00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:47.000
Extraordinary.

cue0017806
00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:49.000
I mean, done this in

cue0017807
00:31:49.000 --> 00:31:51.000
immediate

cue0017808
00:31:51.000 --> 00:31:53.000
after the Holocaust.

cue0017809
00:31:53.000 --> 00:31:55.000
And this is the Mishna.

cue0017810
00:31:55.000 --> 00:31:57.000
In addition,

cue0017811
00:31:57.000 --> 00:31:59.000
they collected

cue0017812
00:31:59.000 --> 00:32:01.000
the epimetrical

cue0017813
00:32:01.000 --> 00:32:03.000
traditions.

cue0017814
00:32:03.000 --> 00:32:05.000
The exegesis.

cue0017815
00:32:05.000 --> 00:32:07.000
The legal exegesis.

cue0017816
00:32:07.000 --> 00:32:09.000
On several books.

cue0017817
00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:11.000
On the book of

cue0017818
00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:13.000
Vayiqraʾ,

cue0017819
00:32:13.000 --> 00:32:15.000
that is called

cue0017820
00:32:15.000 --> 00:32:17.000
Siphraʾ.

cue0017821
00:32:17.000 --> 00:32:19.000
On the book of

cue0017822
00:32:19.000 --> 00:32:21.000
Deḇarim and

cue0017823
00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:23.000
Bamidvar, and that is called Siphre.

cue0017824
00:32:23.000 --> 00:32:25.000
Siphre is the plural.

cue0017825
00:32:25.000 --> 00:32:27.000
Plural means the two books.

cue0017826
00:32:27.000 --> 00:32:29.000
Deḇarim and Bamidvar.

cue0017827
00:32:29.000 --> 00:32:31.000
And another

cue0017828
00:32:31.000 --> 00:32:33.000
Rabbi, not from the school of

cue0017829
00:32:33.000 --> 00:32:35.000
Rabbi 'Aqiba, Rabbi Ishmael,

cue0017830
00:32:35.000 --> 00:32:37.000
he collected the traditions

cue0017831
00:32:37.000 --> 00:32:39.000
on the book of Exodus.

cue0017832
00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:41.000
It's called Lechinta.

cue0017833
00:32:41.000 --> 00:32:43.000
Later on,

cue0017834
00:32:43.000 --> 00:32:45.000
about

cue0017835
00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:47.000
150 years

cue0017836
00:32:47.000 --> 00:32:49.000
later,

cue0017837
00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:51.000
a pupil of Rabbeinu Qadosh,

cue0017838
00:32:51.000 --> 00:32:53.000
he collects the

cue0017839
00:32:53.000 --> 00:32:55.000
exegesis.

cue0017840
00:32:55.000 --> 00:32:57.000
Nothing to do with Halakha.

cue0017841
00:32:57.000 --> 00:32:59.000
And that is

cue0017842
00:32:59.000 --> 00:33:01.000
Bereʾshit Rabban

cue0017843
00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:03.000
on the book of Bereʾshit.

cue0017844
00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:05.000
And then other rabbis did it on the other books.

cue0017845
00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:07.000
Including the

cue0017846
00:33:07.000 --> 00:33:09.000
five Megillot.

cue0017847
00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:11.000
They did it on the five books of the Tora,

cue0017848
00:33:11.000 --> 00:33:13.000
and on the five Megillot, which are

cue0017849
00:33:13.000 --> 00:33:15.000
Esther, Ruth,

cue0017850
00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:17.000
Kohelet,

cue0017851
00:33:17.000 --> 00:33:19.000
Shir ha-Shirim,

cue0017852
00:33:19.000 --> 00:33:21.000
and Echa.

cue0017853
00:33:21.000 --> 00:33:23.000
Now,

cue0017854
00:33:23.000 --> 00:33:25.000
all this were collections

cue0017855
00:33:25.000 --> 00:33:27.000
of traditions

cue0017856
00:33:29.000 --> 00:33:31.000
that they were from the time

cue0017857
00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:33.000
of the Temple, or

cue0017858
00:33:33.000 --> 00:33:35.000
at the time of the Temple, or

cue0017859
00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:37.000
developed

cue0017860
00:33:37.000 --> 00:33:39.000
on the traditions of the Temple.

cue0017861
00:33:39.000 --> 00:33:41.000
In other words, we wanted to preserve

cue0017862
00:33:41.000 --> 00:33:43.000
as much

cue0017863
00:33:43.000 --> 00:33:45.000
as we had from the traditions of the Temple.

cue0017864
00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:47.000
And

cue0017865
00:33:47.000 --> 00:33:49.000
these are

cue0017866
00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:51.000
the great rabbinic texts.

cue0017867
00:33:51.000 --> 00:33:53.000
Again,

cue0017868
00:33:53.000 --> 00:33:55.000
the person,

cue0017869
00:33:55.000 --> 00:33:57.000
the man with the vision

cue0017870
00:33:57.000 --> 00:33:59.000
to do it was a biakiva.

cue0017871
00:33:59.000 --> 00:34:01.000
He began a movement,

cue0017872
00:34:01.000 --> 00:34:03.000
which was completed

cue0017873
00:34:03.000 --> 00:34:05.000
about

cue0017874
00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:07.000
150 years after

cue0017875
00:34:07.000 --> 00:34:09.000
his death.

cue0017876
00:34:09.000 --> 00:34:11.000
No, a little bit later.

cue0017877
00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:13.000
He died about

cue0017878
00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:15.000
the year 135 or 140.

cue0017879
00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:17.000
By

cue0017880
00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:19.000
the year 220,

cue0017881
00:34:19.000 --> 00:34:21.000
already the Mishna

